{
  "id": 243380668,
  "iid": 11700,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "hci_usb: Use endpoint transfer type instead of id",
  "description": "Current packet-hci_usb.c uses endpoint addresses to determine between\nHCI types (command, event, ACL, SCO).  The addresses given are from the\nsample endpoints in the Bluetooth Core Specification (Version 5.3 Vol 4\nPart B Table 2.1) but are not required to be at that address.  The\nspecification does require the endpoint transfer types for each HCI data\ntype: Control endpoint for HCI commands, Interrupt endpoint for HCI\nevents, Bulk endpoints for ACL data, and Isochronous endpoints for SCO\ndata.  So use URB transfer_type instead to determine HCI type.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2023-08-15T19:41:52.280Z",
  "updated_at": "2023-08-25T17:46:10.821Z",
