    {
      "id": "6c4240560566e0018ea9cff601f4490b2550c3ef",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 1514819588,
          "type": null,
          "body": "You might want to extend the commit message with reference to since when the addresses are optional. In Linux kernel patch [Bluetooth: btusb: Do not require hardcoded interface numbers](https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id=c13380a55522bf14e54779a142487c224509db95) I have summarized the change as:\n>     Bluetooth: btusb: Do not require hardcoded interface numbers\n>     \n>     Remove hardcoded interface number check because Bluetooth specification\n>     since version 4.0 only recommends and no longer requires specific\n>     interface numbers.\n>     \n>     While earlier Bluetooth versions, i.e. 2.1 + EDR and 3.0 + HS, contain\n>     required configuration table in Volume 4 - Host Controller Interface\n>     Part B - USB Transport Layer, Bluetooth Core Specification Addendum 2\n>     changes the table from required to recommended configuration.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6496125,
            "username": "desowin",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Tomasz Moń",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/e423f0a8da1eede7f89748e5142d6915e4a636399964d35d888ed95ca85e2b50?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/desowin"
          },
