      "parent_ids": [
        "e08da591eebe1b2e6ba2e20527ebf74bbf5b23fa"
      ],
      "title": "hci_usb: Use endpoint transfer type instead of id",
      "message": "hci_usb: Use endpoint transfer type instead of id\n\nCurrent packet-hci_usb.c uses endpoint addresses to determine between\nHCI types (command, event, ACL, SCO).  The addresses given are from the\nsample endpoints in the Bluetooth Core Specification (Version 5.3 Vol 4\nPart B Table 2.1).  Since Version 4.0 those addresses are recommended\nbut not required.  The specification does require the endpoint transfer\ntypes for each HCI data type: Control endpoint for HCI commands,\nInterrupt endpoint for HCI events, Bulk endpoints for ACL data, and\nIsochronous endpoints for SCO data.  So use URB transfer_type instead\nto determine HCI type.\n",
      "author_name": "Aaron Brice",
      "author_email": "aaron.brice@nikolamotor.com",
      "authored_date": "2023-08-15T12:21:23.000-07:00",
      "committer_name": "Tomasz Moń",
      "committer_email": "desowin@gmail.com",
